The '''2000 UEFA Champions League final''' was a [[Association football|football]] match that took place on 24 May 2000. The match was played at [[Stade de France]] in [[Saint-Denis, Seine-Saint-Denis|Saint-Denis]], France, to determine the winner of the [[1999–2000 UEFA Champions League]]. Spanish teams [[Real Madrid CF|Real Madrid]] (playing in their eleventh final in the competition) and [[Valencia CF|Valencia]] (in their maiden appearance at this stage) were the participants in the first final in the history of the European Cup or Champions League to feature two clubs from the same country.

Real Madrid won the match 3–0 to claim the trophy for a record-extending eighth time.

