==Match==
===Summary===
A headed goal from [[Fernando Morientes]] in the first half and a spectacular [[Steve McManaman]] volley midway through the second half put Real Madrid 2–0 ahead, before [[Raúl (footballer)|Raúl]] sealed the win with a breakaway third goal, rounding [[Santiago Cañizares]] after a Valencia corner was cleared.

The win was Real Madrid's eighth European Cup victory overall and their second in three years, and was notable for being [[Vicente del Bosque]]'s first title as manager. It was also a landmark for being the first final played between two teams from the same nation. Upon this win, McManaman became the first [[English people|English]] player to win the tournament with a non-English club.

